l have the power of mind controling Tumors In second Edtion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T07:37:50-07:00","id":1304620,"title":"","content":"Questions about completing the New Dawn:<br /> <br /> 1) <b>What counts as 'completing a Refinement' when looking at the final outcomes? </b> Completing a single role on a refinement, or completing all 3? Context as well as the example seems to suggest the former, but the wording (complete a <i>Refinement</i> instead of completing a <i>Role from a given Refinement) </i>makes me doubt this.<br /> <br /> 2) The 'final outcome' is a result of the 'Roles she has completed along her pilgrimage' while additional roles 'do not feed in to the result of the Great Work'. It then goes in to talking about how to construct the Redeemed's human history based on those roles within the Pilgrimage. My question here is: <b>does this also apply to the completed refinement chart on the following page?</b> If a given Promethean's Pilgrimage only encompasses 6 refinements, with several roles in each, but they go above and beyond and complete all 10 refinements, are they still restricted to the Refinement 6-7 benefits? This would seem to harshly discourage branching out and learning more during the Pilgrimage if so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T22:01:33-07:00","id":1307143,"title":"","content":"Sanctus Aspiratus Alembic Steal Pyros/Drain Pyros<br /> <br /> Perhaps this was answered some point prior but I couldnt find it so I'm hoping I've found the right place:<br /> <br /> Am I correct in thinking that when you use either Steal Pyros or Drain Pyros if your opponent has a Pyros Pool that is empty do your successes deal the stated Lethal Dmg and for every 2 points do you still receive the 1 point of Pyros or if they do have a Pyros Pool that is empty the Distillation does nothing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","user":"WyrmWeaver","date":".  Typos 04-23-2019, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12936-wyrmweaver","name":"WyrmWeaver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:07:43-07:00","id":1307512,"title":"","content":"From Steal Pyros<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the target has a Pyros pool, the Savant steals Pyros directly. If not, the Promethean inflicts one point of lethal damage per success and absorbs one point of Pyros for every two points of lethal damage inflict\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> And Drain Pyros<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the target doesn't have a Pyros pool, the Promethean can convert Health at the same rate described under Steal Pyros.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like these Sanctus Aspiratus react to a template rather more than anything. \u201cDoes the pyros pool exist?\u201d Not, \u201cis the pyros pool empty?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> From a narrative perspective, my understanding is that if a being has a pyros pool, the divine fire is held in that pool. This is the animating life force, not fully integrated into the form of the creature. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think extracting pyros from flesh requires it to be from a being that is naturally alive, noted by the stipulation that these powers do not work upon the Undead. While Prometheans and Pandorans aren\u2019t undead, they are not natural entities as far as this world is concerned. Their pyros is concentrated in the form of a polluting fuel, hence the risk of disquiet and wastelands. I don\u2019t see these Distillations further attacking health from such a being, as it also doesn\u2019t suck the charge out of another promethean\u2019s distillations (a power from the flux refinement). <br /> <br /> <br /> I do think there are some strange exceptions, however. Alchemists have a pyros pool according to their Magnitude, but it\u2019s described as their ability to store that pyros in external vessels. I think these Distillations would do damage to the alchemist, but you would specifically target the human rather than the vials of glowing liquid on their belt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Analyzing these differences could be a great milestone for a Savant, as they study the variations between vessels of pyros and it\u2019s natural place in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T06:36:28-07:00","id":1310524,"title":"","content":"I m not sure if i read it correctly,<br /> Do you think that the biting aura distillation area of effect is the same as the azothic radiance range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user"