e:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:42:11-08:00","id":1368597,"title":"","content":"From someone unfamiliar with the game: is it possible to play this without following the story thread of becoming human? I don't know how brutal disquiet is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T11:59:42-08:00","id":1368604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1368597#post1368597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From someone unfamiliar with the game: is it possible to play this without following the story thread of becoming human?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, sure. Did you have specific other plans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know how brutal disquiet is. </div> </div> </div>It requires people to roll less successes with two Attributes than you roll on one Trait that you always have the option of reducing to 1, it doesn't advance past &quot;this person is much harder for you to socially influence and may, at your option, attempt to violently remove you from their presence&quot; outside of a highly unlikely roll or in specific chunks of real estate that are more manageable at low levels of that same Trait that you can always reduce to low levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-26T03:35:25-08:00","id":1370523,"title":"","content":"Once a promethean has mastered all the roles of a refinement, can he create multiple athanor with that knowledge or only one?<br /> And if he obtain a regular failure in the athanor creation can he try again, expending again the vitriol exp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T06:35:13-07:00","id":1374119,"title":"","content":"Does pandorans emit Azothic radiance? Core book says that in dormancy they don t, but what about when they re awake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T06:57:12-07:00","id":1374122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1374119#post1374119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does pandorans emit Azothic radiance? Core book says that in dormancy they don t, but what about when they re awake?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't. The bit about them not emitting Azothic radiance in Dormancy is just a point of emphasis on how there's no way to identify a Dormant Pandoran in the Promethean toolkit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T22:41:02-07:00","id":1390709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1370523#post1370523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once a promethean has mastered all the roles of a refinement, can he create multiple athanor with that knowledge or only one?<br /> And if he obtain a regular failure in the athanor creation can he try again, expending again the vitriol exp?</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of phrases like &quot;consumes everything she has passed into the Athanor&quot; and &quot;the Promethean does not empty herself of her understanding [on a dramatic failure],&quot; combined with the fact that exceptional success guarantees you (almost) always have access to the Transmutations of the Refinement, suggests to me that, succeed or fail, attempting to forge an Athanor can only be done once per occasion that you've completed a Refinement; you'd need to reexamine the Roles again to have another shot.<br /> <br /> These are, after all, sources of Vitriol and safety, means of venting Persistent Conditions, ways to conditionally retain eight Alembics for half the price of one, and so on \u2014 chances to make them being few and far between is one of the handful of things incentivizing you to raise your Azoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T12:06:49-07:00","id":1399633,"title":"","content":"Here's a simple question to reinvigorate this thread.<br /> <br /> Is Doomguy an example of a Master of the Refinement of Tin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T19:55:46-07:00","id":1399978,"title":"","content":"Oh and a more serious question. <br /> <br /> With Roles, they are often a more specific take on the overall philosophy of a Refinement. Furies seek to learn how to control their Rage/torment. The Outcast does so through interacting with those on the fringes of society, those like him who he can relate to and learn WHY they are on the fringes (and how that does not make them worthless despite it all). The Savage is the Role that explores the refinement at it's most direct point; lashing out at the world and driving others away, and subsequently quenching that anger and experiencing the loss that comes with it. And finally, the Vigilante seeks to punish those he feels has wronged him/his friends and learning how to dish that need out in a controlled fashion.<br /> <br /> So what's with the Argentum Roles? I understand the Refinement, learn about humanity by seeing how other monsters lack/have lost that humanity they once had. But it seems the Roles simply provide other methods to do that. Basically I dont really see how it's a specified Role. Is learning about how monsters fall by the wayside from humans different when doing so as a Warden rather than an Envoy?<br /> <br /> EDIT: also, does the Savage Role require that the promethean also shun his throng?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-30-2020, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:38:30-07:00","id":1401804,"title":"","content":"Question about Clones &amp; Hybrids - would one build their own Clone/Hybrid antagonists in the same manner as one would a Pandoran? I'm thinking about Revenant equivalents for Promethean but there's no hard and fast info on how they're different from Pandorans. <br /> <br /> Related: Homunculi - was someone still working on house rules for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T04:58:50-07:00","id":1402783,"title":"","content":"Question about Extempore and Saturninus: <br /> <br /> p.38: \u201cThe Matchless don't have the same access to Azothic memory that other Prometheans enjoy, because their Lineage is not represented there.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Plumb the Fathoms Alembic (pp.152\u2013153) is specifically about Azothic memory. Are Extempore forbidden from taking it? If not, how does it work for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T05:50:31-07:00","id":1402790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1402783#post1402783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Extempore and Saturninus: <br /> <br /> p.38: \u201cThe Matchless don't have the same access to Azothic memory that other Prometheans enjoy, because their Lineage is not represented there.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Plumb the Fathoms Alembic (pp.152\u2013153) is specifically about Azothic memory. Are Extempore forbidden from taking it? If not, how does it work for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can use it if they are part of a branded throng with other lineages.<br /> The core book explain it, don t remember where","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T06:54:51-07:00","id":1402800,"title":"","content":"Could someone cite this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-14T08:03:58-07:00","id":1402810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1402790#post1402790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can use it if they are part of a branded throng with other lineages.<br /> The core book explain it, don t remember where</div> </div> </div> </div>Found it, pag 153, the sidebar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T14:14:12-07:00","id":1402982,"title":"","content":"Under the new dawn roll modifiers there is <br /> &quot;The character has met her creator and understands her condition.&quot;<br /> The meaning of this phrase confuses me a little, can someone come up with an example please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-15T15:15:21-07:00","id":1402993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1402982#post1402982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Under the new dawn roll modifiers there is</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The character has met her creator and understands her condition.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The meaning of this phrase confuses me a little, can someone come up with an example please?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Promethean character who knows what they are and has a direct understanding of why they were made is more likely to achieve humanity than one that has simply stumbled through their Refinements on Azothic Memory alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In 1e, your creator was a more likely source of Torment than most things, which was part of the reason Prometheans of an established Lineage tended to part ways with their makers by the time they started to walk the Pilgrimage. That's not hard-coded in 2e, but the difficulties of multiple Prometheans hanging around in one place and the personal nature of the Pilgrimage is such that a higher-Azoth Promethean is unlikely to stick around in a place where they've created a potent Wasteland and another Promethean for very long.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having met the clockmaker who assembled him from spare parts and drunken obsession helps the Unfleshed piece together a little bit more about himself, particularly when he's seen beneath the semblance of a human form he was made with to the oil and springs that keep his heart ticking.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The one-eyed Nepri who's had an opportunity to talk with the one-legged death-seeker who made her about his choice of subtraction would not know herself quite as well if she simply proceeded through her Roles and made a jump for the brass ring.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Extempore lucky enough to be made from a spontaneously-animated statue with a living sculptor may or may not derive some benefit from having insight into his source material's shaping, but it's probably worth finding out, if only for the sake of self-knowledge.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-15-2020, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T03:54:15-07:00","id":1403079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1402993#post1402993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Promethean character who knows what they are and has a direct understanding of why they were made is more likely to achieve humanity than one that has simply stumbled through their Refinements on Azothic Memory alone.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In 1e, your creator was a more likely source of Torment than most things, which was part of the reason Prometheans of an established Lineage tended to part ways with their makers by the time they started to walk the Pilgrimage. That's not hard-coded in 2e, but the difficulties of multiple Prometheans hanging around in one place and the personal nature of the Pilgrimage is such that a higher-Azoth Promethean is unlikely to stick around in a place where they've created a potent Wasteland and another Promethean for very long.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Having met the clockmaker who assembled him from spare parts and drunken obsession helps the Unfleshed piece together a little bit more about himself, particularly when he's seen beneath the semblance of a human form he was made with to the oil and springs that keep his heart ticking.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The one-eyed Nepri who's had an opportunity to talk with the one-legged death-seeker who made her about his choice of subtraction would not know herself quite as well if she simply proceeded through her Roles and made a jump for the brass ring.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:HelveticaNeue\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Extempore lucky enough to be made from a spontaneously-animated statue with a living sculptor may or may not derive some benefit from having insight into his source material's shaping, but it's probably worth finding out, if only for the sake of self-knowledge.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but the terms of &quot;understanding her conditions&quot; are a little vague.<br /> Would you consider completing a Plumbum role as a sufficient requisite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T11:01:32-07:00","id":1403121,"title":"","content":"So the sidebar on 153 suggests Extempore gain access to the Azothic Memory for the purposes of Transmutations and other powers if they have the Branded Throng Condition. Does this also give them access to Elpis Visions and other things rooted in Azothic Memory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T11:31:29-07:00","id":1403128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1403121#post1403121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the sidebar on 153 suggests Extempore gain access to the Azothic Memory for the purposes of Transmutations and other powers if they have the Branded Throng Condition. Does this also give them access to Elpis Visions and other things rooted in Azothic Memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the sidebar says any power, so i think yes.<br /> By the way i m not sure if elpis visions require azothic memory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T22:53:22-07:00","id":1406386,"title":"","content":"I am a little confused on the Disquiet procedure (p. 173). I just want to talk through it to make sure I'm reading it correctly...<br /> <br /> When an NPC is exposed to a Disquiet trigger, the Storyteller makes a roll for the NPC: R+C vs. Promethean's Azoth.<br /> <br /> If the Storyteller rolls a Dramatic Failure for the NPC, it says the <b><i>player </i></b>gains the Disquieted Condition at one stage higher than normal. Is this a typo? They're not referring to the Promethean, are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T23:17:15-07:00","id":1406389,"title":"","content":"It should say victim, yes. The NPC, not the Promethean, gains the Disquieted Condition at one stage higher than normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T00:29:29-07:00","id":1406394,"title":"","content":"Do you think there is a way to learn a complex refinement from Petrificati?<br /> Studying them in their roles for example, or talking to one who was originally a Promethean who mastered the stucked role?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:14:18-07:00","id":1406498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1406394#post1406394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think there is a way to learn a complex refinement from Petrificati?<br /> Studying them in their roles for example, or talking to one who was originally a Promethean who mastered the stucked role?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont believe so. Prtrificati are just drones with very limited responses. I would be like trying to learn world history from a book that only talks about one country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:25:28-07:00","id":1406502,"title":"","content":"More to the point, Petrificati are just imitating their roles: if you can learn from them, you can learn from other Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T19:52:55-07:00","id":1406720,"title":"","content":"Rekindle their Azoth and (re)start their Pilgrimage. They would definitely have a very interesting perspective.<br /> <br /> Find a Tormented Petrificatus (if they exist) and study how supernatural anguish interacts with mindlessness. Might give some insight into Stannum.<br /> <br /> FInd one created by the Stasher, as they would have an Athanor sewn inside them. Careful, they tend to be possessive of them in ways other Stuck never are.<br /> <br /> The Collector has created an entire &quot;village&quot; of Petrificati, each with a different Role. As he gains more, they begin to act more human. Is it the same mindlessness, or is it something more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23990-gizmit","name":"Gizmit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23990_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T04:44:51-07:00","id":1414353,"title":"","content":"Can a promethean use the Lightning therapy distillation on itself?<br /> I know that by raw the answer is probably not, but i cannot understand the logic of this.<br /> The power converts pyros in a healing current, it s not a health level transfer, so why it shouldn t work on the user body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T08:13:14-07:00","id":1414405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1414353#post1414353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a promethean use the Lightning therapy distillation on itself?<br /> I know that by raw the answer is probably not, but i cannot understand the logic of this.<br /> The power converts pyros in a healing current, it s not a health level transfer, so why it shouldn t work on the user body?</div> </div> </div> </div>The user's body already benefits from the Persistent effect of the Alembic. The normal effects of healing with electricity are that you can spend Pyros while already healing to heal more, whereas Lightning Therapy doesn't even deal electrical damage and the Promethean is actively channeling her energies to accomplish the effect.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spend one Pyros to allow you to heal without an electrical current at triple the rate an electrical current would allow you to heal by spending Pyros&quot; is also a bit much for a Distillation immediately succeeded by &quot;you can draw power from electrical currents that you aren't directly touching&quot; and &quot;you gain temporary Health boxes for the scene.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T09:41:03-07:00","id":1414414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1414405#post1414405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The user's body already benefits from the Persistent effect of the Alembic. The normal effects of healing with electricity are that you can spend Pyros while already healing to heal more, whereas Lightning Therapy doesn't even deal electrical damage and the Promethean is actively channeling her energies to accomplish the effect.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Spend one Pyros to allow you to heal without an electrical current at triple the rate an electrical current would allow you to heal by spending Pyros&amp;quot; is also a bit much for a Distillation immediately succeeded by &amp;quot;you can draw power from electrical currents that you aren't directly touching&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;you gain temporary Health boxes for the scene.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in comparision to the other distillation of the alambic it would be unbalanced, i agree.<br /> I only think that it s a bit odd being able to heal others with pyros while only receiving a small boost to natural regeneration for itself.<br /> I would find the first distillation more logic and balanced if it was like<br /> &quot;You can spend n pyros, the target or yourself heals as if it has spent n pyros while under electroshock therapy&quot;<br /> Do anyone are of the same advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T03:27:22-07:00","id":1418975,"title":"","content":"If i understand it rightly basic refinements are learned through azothic memory.<br /> Does this mean that an extempore without a branded throng can learn them only with a teacher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T22:44:55-08:00","id":1428155,"title":"","content":"Can Flux alembics be calcified? Asking for a friend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T00:09:21-08:00","id":1428161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1428155#post1428155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Flux alembics be calcified? Asking for a friend</div> </div> </div> </div>Suure, buddy. That's what every Hundred-Handed amalgamation of limbs and maws says. Asking for a friend.<br /> <br /> Centimani can't make normal vitriol expenditures, so they can't calcify alembics, and other Prometheans don't have access to Flux alembics to try to calcify. The Mutation alembic, however, allows Centimani to calcify Pandoran Dread Powers, and they stay calcified even if the Promethean later adopts a Refinement and sheds Flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T23:14:18-08:00","id":1428237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1428161#post1428161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Suure, buddy. That's what every Hundred-Handed amalgamation of limbs and maws says. Asking for a friend.<br /> <br /> Centimani can't make normal vitriol expenditures, so they can't calcify alembics, and other Prometheans don't have access to Flux alembics to try to calcify. The Mutation alembic, however, allows Centimani to calcify Pandoran Dread Powers, and they stay calcified even if the Promethean later adopts a Refinement and sheds Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much kind sir!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T14:32:35-08:00","id":1431214,"title":"","content":"After a conversation with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> , i developed a dark eras variation of the Machinus Alembic.<br /> Feel free to comment about utility and scientific accuracy.<br /> <br /> Sidereus (Machinus) <br /> <br /> The Sidereus Alembic is the pre-industrial version of Machinus. In the past the Alembic had identical powers, but the Azothic memory instructed Promethean on alternative uses focused on interactions with metals, expecially iron and steel. <br /> <br /> Persistent: The Promethean gentles her humours, rendering them sensitive to the electrical flow of the world around her. She senses electrical energy, magnetic fields (usually natural magnets or Degaussed prometheans) and conductive materials (usually metals) within 200 yards, along with their relative strength or quantity. At Storyteller\u2019s discretion, particularly powerful sources of electrical energy can be detected up to fifty miles away. The Promethean also instinctively knows where natural lightning will likely strike within the next few minutes. <br /> <br /> Lodestone <br /> Running an electrical current through his body, the Promethean may grasp a metallic item and power it. <br /> Cost: 1 Pyros <br /> Dice Pool: None <br /> Action: Reflexive <br /> The Promethean must remain close enough to touch the object, maintaining a constant flow of electricity. He doesn\u2019t have to remain in absolute contact \u2014 standing in front of an armored soldier will do \u2014 but he must be able to touch the item without effort. While within range of this power, a conductive material can be heated like if it was on a campfire.<br /> A ferromagnetic metal can also be turned in a weak magnet (no more than Strenght 1) that lasts until the electrical flow stops.<br /> The promethean can change at will the orientation of the magnetic field (this can be used to convey simple information to an user of the Persistent effect in range, like a direction or a yes/no). <br /> <br /> Heaven's fire <br /> The Promethean may effortlessly send Electricity through the air to a conductive target. By means of this Transmutation, a Promethean may remotely use Lodestone on an item, as if she\u2019s using the power while in contact with it. <br /> Cost: 2 Pyros <br /> Dice Pool: None <br /> Action: Reflexive <br /> A Promethean may apply any effect of Lodestone on an appropriate target within sight range (to a maximum of 200 yards). She can roughly determine which type of metal the target is made of by measuring its electrical interaction properties.<br /> If she chooses to physically grasp a metallic item, she may raise its temperature up to 12,5 Celsius degrees per turn.<br /> By touching a ferromagnetic object, she can turn it into a strong magnet or increase its natural magnetism (up to Azoth in Strenght score) while the power lasts.<br /> Her control over the magnetic field intensity paired with Azothic memory instructions allows her to convey Pilgrim Marks to other prometheans in range capable of feeling them.<br /> Alternately, if the Promethean is capable of remotely sharing Pyros (through the Vulcanus or Benefice Transmutations), while using Electroshock Therapy she can fill her throng with Pyros or heal them from afar. <br /> <br /> Forge of the Gods<br /> At the apex of Sidereus, the Promethean can use his control over electricity to enhance metalworking and encode complex texts in magnetic fields.<br /> Also she doesn\u2019t have to physically see an item to power it; if he senses the target via the Persistent effect, he may now use Heaven's fire effects on it without a roll.<br /> Cost: 3 Pyros <br /> Action: Instant <br /> Dice Pool: Manipulation + Crafts (or Enigmas if writing informations) + Azoth <br /> Roll Results <br /> Dramatic Failure: The power fails to work, and the crafted item gains the Fragile condition.<br /> Written informations deteriorates quickly or conveys false statements.<br /> Failure: The power fails to work. <br /> Success: The Promethean can direct precisely an electrical flow into the target for the remainder of the scene, as if he held it in her hand. <br /> He can alter the magnetic field of a ferromagnetic item in order to temporary &quot;write&quot; complex encoded information (one sentence or one uncolored sketched picture per point of Intelligence) and the message can be changed with a following instant action.<br /> Other Prometheans using this Distillation can access the information while in range.<br /> It is also possible to activate the power at the beginning of a metal crafting action (performed by the promethean or by someone else) to apply one special permanent effect to the item.<br /> The crafting still requires a roll, but with a +3 bonus. <br /> The item could receive a permanent free dot in Availability (that translates in a better quality or finely decorated equipment).<br /> A ferromagnetic metal can be made into a natural magnet (maximum Strenght is the lower of Azoth and half of the item size, rounded up) or be permanently encoded with a message (with the same above limits).<br /> Exceptional Success: A written message can be a page long, or a picture very detailed.<br /> Crafted items can be made with two free dots of availability,<br /> The Strenght limit of a crafted natural magnet use the lower of Azoth and Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T18:28:22-08:00","id":1431234,"title":"","content":"Could I ask you to repost this in its own thread? It deserves to be there, rather than buried on page 10 of a thread that covers a wide range of topics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T01:02:12-08:00","id":1431261,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"