inally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1438185#post1438185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, guys. About to start a chronicle in ancient Egypt. Is there an alternative revision for Electrification? I imagine there isn't much else to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ve tried to make an alternative version of the Machinus alembic<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas\"> Machinus ideas - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hi, i m trying to discover a clever usage for the Promethean Machinus powers in a medieval tech setting. I don t want to alter the way the power works, and i m writing this here because i need someone who is more familiar with how electricity behave than to promethean rules. If you don t have access to Promethean 2ed core book the Machinus power works in that way: -Passive ability In a 200 yard radius you can feel electricity and gauge its strenght, the presence of electronics (even unpowered) Very powerful electrical sources can extend the range. Predicts where a lightning will strike within some </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T13:11:24-08:00","id":1438607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1438211#post1438211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ve tried to make an alternative version of the Machinus alembic<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1421755-machinus-ideas\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...machinus-ideas</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that seems very good! I'll take a good read of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T19:36:04-08:00","id":1439582,"title":"","content":"Remind me:<br /> <br /> So IIRC when it comes to any Promethean that are made and rise from a corpse (most obviously the Frankensteins), the text has been clear that said Promethean is NOT the person who originally died<br /> <br /> But...is there a way for said Promethean to perhaps remember or regain said memories? As in, remembering them in full, not just the occasional out of context flash of disconnected memories? Or is it that, the moment the Promethean rises, all those old memories are gone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T21:27:12-08:00","id":1439591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1439582#post1439582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind me:<br /> <br /> So IIRC when it comes to any Promethean that are made and rise from a corpse (most obviously the Frankensteins), the text has been clear that said Promethean is NOT the person who originally died<br /> <br /> But...is there a way for said Promethean to perhaps remember or regain said memories? As in, remembering them in full, not just the occasional out of context flash of disconnected memories? Or is it that, the moment the Promethean rises, all those old memories are gone?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;re-&quot; in gaining those memories \u2014 the Promethean is a new individual made from the pieces of the old person, and the thematics of clone creation suggest that having those pieces be big enough to be discrete parts is a necessary element of making a working proto-soul out of a dead body for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Filling in the gaps in a body's sense-memories is almost certainly going to require secondary sources, whether that's ghosts or old-fashioned legwork to find records. Disconnected bits might exist in somewhat large chunks, but those are materials reworked into the Created being just like the bones and organs and stitching; you might as well ask if there was a way for a vampire to &quot;remember in full&quot; the snatches of rogue personality that accompany the act of diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T19:32:50-08:00","id":1439768,"title":"","content":"Yeah; the Robocop thing of \u201cI am Alex Murphy\u201d is more of a Deviant concept than a Promethean one. Promethean is inspired more by Pinocchio's \u201cI want to be a real boy\u201d concept. <br /> <br /> With that in mind: even if a Promethean <i>did</i> somehow gain the memories of the person who the body formerly belonged to, I'm pretty sure that the result would be more like the memories exchanged by ghosts in Geist 2e: you can access the memory and learn from it; but you know deep down that it's <i>someone else's</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T20:29:02-07:00","id":1439968,"title":"","content":"These answers are not entirely true. While the Promethean is an entirely new person, there are two Merits in the core book that do represent retaining memories of the body's previous/original consciousness.<br /> <br /> Good Brain amounts to utilizing muscle memory, though there is no rule to say it can't use apply to Mental skill.<br /> <br /> Residual Memory is exactly that: the book even calls it tapping into your &quot;past lives.&quot; It comes with negative mental Conditions when used from the body's past traumas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T21:05:35-07:00","id":1439970,"title":"","content":"That's true; and both Satchel's and my answers included that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T21:33:44-07:00","id":1450277,"title":"","content":"Do persistant effects like Vitalitys Unbowed cap at Azoth attribute maximums.","si