 them anymore Does that mean their now a valid encounter for hunters in a crossover game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-18-2021, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:07:44-07:00","id":1461753,"title":"","content":"&quot;each Promethean has a specific path through the Refinements in front of her&quot; pg296<br /> <br /> Do Roles and Refinements need to be done in a specific order? If so, what happens if a Role is done before its time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T05:29:26-07:00","id":1461941,"title":"","content":"Roles can be done in any order to complete the pilgrimage, though you do have the limitations of when you can do roles in complex refinements (can't have more complex refinements than basic)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T06:10:44-07:00","id":1461947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1461941#post1461941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roles can be done in any order to complete the pilgrimage, though you do have the limitations of when you can do roles in complex refinements (can't have more complex refinements than basic)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this applies on the overall Pilgrimage, not at any given moment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T06:17:49-07:00","id":1461949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1461753#post1461753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;each Promethean has a specific path through the Refinements in front of her&amp;quot; pg296<br /> <br /> Do Roles and Refinements need to be done in a specific order? If so, what happens if a Role is done before its time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that unless a Role has another one as a &quot;prerequisite&quot; you can complete them in any order.<br /> If you are not ready for an &quot;advanced&quot; role, you would simply fail to complete it, and Elpis visions would guide you to the required &quot;prerequisite&quot; Role","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T16:59:06-07:00","id":1462598,"title":"","content":"So, quick question: How much Vitriol XP would a player generally &quot;earn&quot; compared to normal XP?<br /> <br /> To give an example, if a player over the course of a chronicle has earned 10 &quot;normal&quot; XP, how much Vitriol XP would they have by that point? I'm asking as someone who has never actually played PtC before, but might ST it sometime in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T03:37:29-08:00","id":1468110,"title":"","content":"Soooo making Alchemist characters for a game, and I'd like to know: since Alchemists get their powers by picking Distillations rather than full Alembics, how do they do with Alembic's persistant effects? Do they just not get these? Do they have to buy them as individual Distillations? Or do they automatically get them as long as they got Distillations in the matching Alembic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T05:10:15-08:00","id":1468114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1468110#post1468110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo making Alchemist characters for a game, and I'd like to know: since Alchemists get their powers by picking Distillations rather than full Alembics, how do they do with Alembic's persistant effects? Do they just not get these? Do they have to buy them as individual Distillations? Or do they automatically get them as long as they got Distillations in the matching Alembic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use the last option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T05:01:46-08:00","id":1468341,"title":"","content":"Alright, thanks Neos01. I guess I will use that option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T17:09:34-08:00","id":1469046,"title":"","content":"For Firestorm aftermath, what does this mean?<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Wasteland effects on the Firestorm\u2019s area of effect immediately end.&quot;<br /> <br /> A wasteland is wiped out when a Firestorm ends anyway, no? So there is no Wasteland and this triggers after the Firestorm is done, so what effects are there to end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T18:36:39-08:00","id":1469055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1469046#post1469046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Firestorm aftermath, what does this mean?<br /> <br /> &quot;\u2022 Wasteland effects on the Firestorm\u2019s area of effect immediately end.&quot;<br /> <br /> A wasteland is wiped out when a Firestorm ends anyway, no? So there is no Wasteland and this triggers after the Firestorm is done, so what effects are there to end?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wasteland ends. Its effects, including reduced Structure and Durability of objects and effective bashing damage on mortals, do not <i>immediately</i> end, and may be tipped over the edge into more severe damage depending on the Aspects of the Firestorm. Just because the Unfleshed pilgrim burned out the Festering mess in their apartment complex doesn't mean the thin coating of oil on everything vanishes overnight.<br /> <br /> Also, given that this is a possible outcome for a completely different category of Firestorm trigger than the one produced through exacerbating a Wasteland, &quot;the Wasteland ends&quot; is clearly not an intrinsic property of Wastelands in Firestorms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-27-2021, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T20:03:42-08:00","id":1469064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1469055#post1469055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, given that this is a possible outcome for a completely different category of Firestorm trigger than the one produced through exacerbating a Wasteland, &quot;the Wasteland ends&quot; is clearly not an intrinsic property of Wastelands in Firestorms.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Clearly&quot; seems a strange word to use here: the mention of Firestorms in the &quot;Wasteland&quot; section explicitly says they clear away a Wasteland and may be triggered towards that end. And the &quot;Firestorms&quot; section twice says that they clear away Wastelands and one of those times explains that this is a reason Prometheans may want to trigger one on purpose. It is hardly &quot;clear&quot; that this is not something that happens every time. In fact, I would say it's clear that it does clear Wastelands every time; there is no place that says it does not.<br /> <br /> I also cannot find anywhere that says that the reduced Structure/Durability are lingering?<br /> <br /> Mostly, I'm curious where the text supports this interpretation, as I didn't get the same interpretation at all in reading it today.<br /> <br /> Still, thank you for your quick response in a mostly-empty forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T05:58:34-08:00","id":1469090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1469064#post1469064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Clearly&quot; seems a strange word to use here: the mention of Firestorms in the &quot;Wasteland&quot; section explicitly says they clear away a Wasteland and may be triggered towards that end.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says the reverse: that you can deliberately call down a Firestorm to clear a Wasteland, which the mechanics establish by &quot;Firestorm&quot; being the final category of Wasteland advancement, which may be deliberately triggered by enacting enough Festering triggers to get it to that level. Firestorms can happen without a Wasteland being involved at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also cannot find anywhere that says that the reduced Structure/Durability are lingering? </div> </div> </div>They don't set in immediately \u2014 they're applied to stuff brought into the area over the course of the first day \u2014 and the destructive impact of many Aspects makes it a moot point a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the &quot;Firestorms&quot; section twice says that they clear away Wastelands and one of those times explains that this is a reason Prometheans may want to trigger one on purpose. It is hardly &quot;clear&quot; that this is not something that happens every time. In fact, I would say it's clear that it does clear Wastelands every time; there is no place that says it does not. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Firestorm&quot; section in Chapter Two also says that Disquiet is banished in the wake of a Firestorm despite &quot;Disquiet is either ended or triggered&quot; being a starting quality listed under the Azothic Element held by Wasteland Festering-induced Semnai Firestorms.<br /> <br /> The description of Firestorm Catalyst Athanors, also in Chapter Two, says they can be used to set off a Firestorm with a &quot;slightly improved&quot; chance of cleansing a Wasteland, which wouldn't make much sense if Firestorms consistently cleansed Wastelands.<br /> <br /> The Firestorm section's opening text describes them killing Pandorans, and while a Level 4 Extreme Environment can certainly accomplish that, most Firestorms last less than ten turns, most Pandorans will have at least two dots of Stamina, and &quot;all Pandorans take aggravated damage&quot; is a starting effect listed under Lilithian Element Firestorms.<br /> <br /> The subsection on Scale provides the example of qashmallim manifesting with either centered or widespread Firestorms, which allows for the possibility of a Firestorm only clearing out part of a Wasteland.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Firestorm section emphasizes the unpredictability of Firestorms \u2014 there's the breadth of Aspects they can possess along with the usual note on the list of example triggers that that list is neither exhaustive nor guaranteed \u2014 and provides mechanics that all but guarantee a Firestorm triggered by a Promethean Festering a Wasteland to the fifth stage will have enough Strength to apply at least two aftereffects from the list that includes clearing Wasteland effects, ending Disquiet, and severely damaging Pandorans.<br /> <br /> It's Pyros. It's volatile and made of change, and a Firestorm is undirected change at that. You can try to stack the deck, but there are no guarantees when playing with the Divine Fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T15:39:27-08:00","id":1471954,"title":"","content":"What would be a reasonable rate of switching refinements? All I've got is that you can change it as many times you want - but how does it work, really? Can a promethean change it reflexively, once every turn, during combat, once per day, once per chapter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-06T16:44:01-08:00","id":1471966,"title":"","content":"In 1e at least, changing refinements took roughly a week with a mentor or a month without. Except when switching to Stannum in particular, which was immediate (the way it's phrased in the book implies but doesn't state that it's reflexive), and changing <i>out</i> of Stannum to anything else, which took twice as long as it would usually take. Refinements work a bit differently in 2e and I don't think it's stated in the book (which would explain why you can't find it), but you could probably use those numbers as rough guidelines or at least starting points - maybe roughly a chapter/week for a simple refinement at least, to start with (except Stannum).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 01-06-2022, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T18:02:43-08:00","id":1476012,"title":"","content":"In the Benefice transmutation (PtC 2e, pg. 123), the &quot;Able Worker&quot; Distillation of the Command Alembic and the Bulwark Distillation of the Control Alembic are identical except for their Pyros cost. Has this been addressed anywhere? Is it intentional? For that matter, is there an official errata collection somewhere I could check for things like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7058-kerredai","name":"Kerredai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T18:15:31-08:00","id":1476015,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is a version difference, but the copy I'm checking has Able Worker issue Inspired (easier exceptional successes and gain Willpower) and Bulwark issue Steadfast (upgrade a failure to a success).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T18:18:07-08:00","id":1476016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerredai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476012#post1476012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Benefice transmutation (PtC 2e, pg. 123), the &quot;Able Worker&quot; Distillation of the Command Alembic and the Bulwark Distillation of the Control Alembic are identical except for their Pyros cost. Has this been addressed anywhere? Is it intentional? For that matter, is there an official errata collection somewhere I could check for things like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check that you have the Final Download version of the PDF, because the difference between those two is that one gives the Inspired Condition (resolve to make a roll count as an exceptional success on three successes and regain one point of Willpower) and the other gives the Steadfast Condition (resolve to turn a failed roll into a roll with one success or turn a chance die into a single regular die).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T21:56:20-08:00","id":1476079,"title":"","content":"Would a Bestowment about having items attached to or stored within a Unfleshed be appropriate? It's a common trope that robots have weapons and items actually attached to them, and I think having a internal cell phone or computer might be interesting.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, would the Electromagnetic Linguistics merit from Demon be appropriate to pull over?<br /> <br /> Edit: There seems to have been a error on the site, that prevented this post from updating the most recent post for Promethean. I will be testing to see if a edit or a new post fixes the error. I will try to come up with a new question for the new post if this edit doesn\u2019t work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-09-2022, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T08:40:19-08:00","id":1476096,"title":"","content":"The edit didn\u2019t work. Let see about a new question.<br /> <br /> What would be the appropriate refinement for a Promethean that\u2019s just trying to understand the natural world? This would be a for a starter character who just woke up without any humans around.<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, now the general front page is sporting yesterday\u2019s post, while the Promethean front page is correct\u2026I can live with that.<br /> Edit 2: and now both are fixed,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-09-2022, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T09:45:42-08:00","id":1476099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476079#post1476079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Bestowment about having items attached to or stored within a Unfleshed be appropriate? It's a common trope that robots have weapons and items actually attached to them, and I think having a internal cell phone or computer might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's certainly a thematic option, though having a single built-in tool is kind of a cooked noodle for what a Bestowment represents. Maybe something on par with Hidden Compartments or Integrate Technology from Deviant would be appropriate, or else modeled as a Merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:07:47-08:00","id":1476103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476099#post1476099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's certainly a thematic option, though having a single built-in tool is kind of a cooked noodle for what a Bestowment represents. Maybe something on par with Hidden Compartments or Integrate Technology from Deviant would be appropriate, or else modeled as a Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, the Integrate Technology is more what I want from the power rather than Hidden Compartments mechanically. Though modeling the power as a merit is certainly interesting. Maybe merit dots equal to size? Should the Bestowment/Merit replicate Integrate Technology and \u201cfeed\u201d power or ammo or whatever to the object?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476099#post1476099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kind of a cooked noodle</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not heard this expression before. Do you mean it\u2019s too flexible? Or it\u2019s not enough by itself for a meal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T10:22:02-08:00","id":1476105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476103#post1476103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not heard this expression before. Do you mean it\u2019s too flexible? Or it\u2019s not enough by itself for a meal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I misunderstood your original proposition and assumed you meant the Promethean would have a single tool upon which they could call, which would be somewhat less dazzling than turning into a swarm of nanobots or coming back from death.<br /> <br /> I think, yes, in such a case an integrated tool would most likely be fueled by the Divine Fire within the Created. Perhaps you could have the character spend a point of Pyros to generate a full charge for an object, whether that means a powered battery or a fresh clip of bullets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T14:01:01-08:00","id":1476115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476096#post1476096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The edit didn\u2019t work. Let see about a new question.<br /> <br /> What would be the appropriate refinement for a Promethean that\u2019s just trying to understand the natural world? This would be a for a starter character who just woke up without any humans around.<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, now the general front page is sporting yesterday\u2019s post, while the Promethean front page is correct\u2026I can live with that.<br /> Edit 2: and now both are fixed,</div> </div> </div> </div>Cuprum, all roles<br /> Also, both the transmutations are really useful for surviving in the nature","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T15:06:53-08:00","id":1476121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1476079#post1476079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a Bestowment about having items attached to or stored within a Unfleshed be appropriate? It's a common trope that robots have weapons and items actually attached to them, and I think having a internal cell phone or computer might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>1e represented this with the Device (\u2022\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit introduced in Saturnine Night alongside the Unfleshed (p59). It was character-creation-only and revealed the character's disfigurements whenever it was used, which would definitely be reasonable to port as a Bestowment in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T21:29:21-07:00","id":1479392,"title":"","content":"What would be a good Humour for a Extempore that was made from a Eidolon? Mana? <br /> <br /> Would it be too crippling for the bestowment of such a creature to cause Quiescence and Dissonance when revealing their disfigurements? Ie taking damage if a Sleeper sees their true form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T22:08:33-07:00","id":1479394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479392#post1479392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a good Humour for a Extempore that was made from a Eidolon? Mana?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tass, if we're to get something that can be engaged with on Promethean's terms, though the particulars will boil down to who made the Eidolon and how and why. In practical terms, you're going to want to know how the humour influences the Extempore's Torment and Wasteland. In thematic terms, the book states plainly that humours should have some connection to the natural or elemental world and the human experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it be too crippling for the bestowment of such a creature to cause Quiescence and Dissonance when revealing their disfigurements? Ie taking damage if a Sleeper sees their true form. </div> </div> </div>That would heavily depend upon what the Bestowment actually does; it could be a perfectly valid balancing cost or needless complication for something that is now only Supernal magic in vaguely technical terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T22:18:40-07:00","id":1479397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479392#post1479392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be a good Humour for a Extempore that was made from a Eidolon? Mana?<br /> <br /> Would it be too crippling for the bestowment of such a creature to cause Quiescence and Dissonance when revealing their disfigurements? Ie taking damage if a Sleeper sees their true form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we're using Extempores, I'd might as well go further and make Path- or even Nimbus-specific arrangements for Humours. Maybe an Aethereal Extempore has molten gold flowing in its veins, and an Arcadian Extempore has liquid silver lining its respiratory tracts.<br /> <br /> I'd rather tie Quiescence and Dissonance with Disquiet, and tie Bestowments with Attainments instead. Maybe something like Mage Sight, or Counterspell. No clues on how'd that actually work though... hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T09:37:56-07:00","id":1479428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479394#post1479394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tass, if we're to get something that can be engaged with on Promethean's terms, though the particulars will boil down to who made the Eidolon and how and why. In practical terms, you're going to want to know how the humour influences the Extempore's Torment and Wasteland. In thematic terms, the book states plainly that humours should have some connection to the natural or elemental world and the human experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Wasteland seemed easy to me. It should be symbolically associated with Truth, and the Supernal bleeding into reality, in a destructive way. So in Sleepers it causes bubbles of intense self delusion, and in everyone else should gain a mage like obsession with understanding mysteries from murders to the stranger things caused by the Wasteland. Physically, it starts empowering and intensify minor supernatural elements and drawing in monsters who feel the wasteland as beacon. It doesn\u2019t actually empower them to make the journey, but it makes them want to. Maybe at High levels it opens a Verge or something equally scary. <br /> <br /> Torment is harder, since Tass and Mana don\u2019t really do anything by themselves when inside someone, usually. Let\u2019s see, how would having too much Truth juice manifest\u2026getting extremely bogged down by the details and getting massively overwhelmed? Hyper fixating on some trivial, yet true facts as absolutely critical to the pilgrimage? Growing Zealous and believing that they know everything they need to to proceed and don\u2019t need to learn anything from anyone\u2026I like that last one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479394#post1479394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would heavily depend upon what the Bestowment actually does; it could be a perfectly valid balancing cost or needless complication for something that is now only Supernal magic in vaguely technical terms.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly, I came up with the idea from the logic of spells take damage from Dissonance, this is something like a living spell, should take damage from Dissonance. I can\u2019t think of anything that\u2019s both thematic and powerful enough to be worth that kind of drawback. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479397#post1479397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're using Extempores, I'd might as well go further and make Path- or even Nimbus-specific arrangements for Humours. Maybe an Aethereal Extempore has molten gold flowing in its veins, and an Arcadian Extempore has liquid silver lining its respiratory tracts.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s so cool. I\u2019m probably going to stick with Tass for now, but if I run into too much of a dead end, I\u2019ll come back for this. Since the creator is most likely a Mastigos, that would be iron\u2026or technically mercury, I guess. I think I like Mercury\u2019s symbolism better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479397#post1479397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather tie Quiescence and Dissonance with Disquiet, and tie Bestowments with Attainments instead. Maybe something like Mage Sight, or Counterspell. No clues on how'd that actually work though... hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, actually Mage Sight would be interesting. I kinda had an idea for a background of being made to observe and record Mysteries that the creator couldn\u2019t reach thanks to politics (and being a lich). That fits rather well. No idea on how to do it though. I think I will move Quiescence and Dissonance to Disquiet, it fits much better there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T17:27:06-07:00","id":1479455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479428#post1479428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Wasteland seemed easy to me. It should be symbolically associated with Truth, and the Supernal bleeding into reality, in a destructive way. So in Sleepers it causes bubbles of intense self delusion, and in everyone else should gain a mage like obsession with understanding mysteries from murders to the stranger things caused by the Wasteland. Physically, it starts empowering and intensify minor supernatural elements and drawing in monsters who feel the wasteland as beacon. It doesn\u2019t actually empower them to make the journey, but it makes them want to. Maybe at High levels it opens a Verge or something equally scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that comes to mind for me is the consequences of using Mastery of Prime to create a Hallow where one was not \u2014 the Extempore tilts the environment around them towards having unique features or being extremely the type of environment that it is.<br /> <br /> The Eidolon's Wasteland twists the Resonance of their surroundings more than usual, subtly warping reality to reflect the flaws of themself and their creator; their Torment might reflect or reject the purpose for which they were created, like one of the Unfleshed; their Disquiet likewise might do as the Ulgans' does and trigger a rising awareness of inconsistencies in the victims' day-to-day lives that they either push to the back of their minds or correctly identify as being the Promethean's fault for incorrect reasons.<br /> <br /> The really easy connection, of course, is to go Abyssal with the motifs as a knock-on effect of the Divine Fire making a piece of Supernal magic go off in unplanned directions over a long period of time. Things don't add up as the Angels command the world in nonsensical directions and the automaton behind it all retreats into its original task, becomes mired in introspection, or becomes increasingly fixated on securing its power over the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T19:35:45-07:00","id":1479464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479455#post1479455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that comes to mind for me is the consequences of using Mastery of Prime to create a Hallow where one was not \u2014 the Extempore tilts the environment around them towards having unique features or being extremely the type of environment that it is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, hadn\u2019t thought of the similarities to a Hallow. That\u2019s probably a better foundation to base stuff off of. Which brings me to a kinda obvious realization in retrospect. The Promethean actually is going to be something like a Hallow, since they will produce Tass as their blood. I wonder how much blood constitutes 1 mana\u2026probably better not to grow down that route. Anyways, the Promethean absolutely should twist the resonance around as a result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479455#post1479455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Eidolon's Wasteland twists the Resonance of their surroundings more than usual, subtly warping reality to reflect the flaws of themself and their creator;</div> </div> </div> </div> The creator is a Ascend first, apologize never type of Mage. That type of Wasteland is going to be *fun* for whoever is inside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479455#post1479455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">their Torment might reflect or reject the purpose for which they were created, like one of the Unfleshed; their Disquiet likewise might do as the Ulgans' does and trigger a rising awareness of inconsistencies in the victims' day-to-day lives that they either push to the back of their minds or correctly identify as being the Promethean's fault for incorrect reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not sure if I agree with the Torment, as I think that the Humors of Extempores rarely allow a similar Torments even when they match an established linage. I\u2019m just not seeing a overabundance of Tass as being that similar to a overabundance of Oil. The Promethean was made for a purpose, true, but I don\u2019t think Tass would reinforce what it was, just was it is currently. I don\u2019t know, that\u2019s how I feel. Hmm\u2026There was a linage of Prophets right? What was their torment? Maybe we can use them?<br /> <br /> The Disquiet is pretty great idea though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479455#post1479455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The really easy connection, of course, is to go Abyssal with the motifs as a knock-on effect of the Divine Fire making a piece of Supernal magic go off in unplanned directions over a long period of time. Things don't add up as the Angels command the world in nonsensical directions and the automaton behind it all retreats into its original task, becomes mired in introspection, or becomes increasingly fixated on securing its power over the world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Certainly a direction we can go with. Hmm. Torment adding a Abyssal motif as the Promethean loses it\u2019s grip on understanding the truth is actually quite fitting.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh did your tag change? If that means you finished Hunter 1e, congratulations! Sorry if I was unobservant and that changed forever ago, or if I am seeing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-24-2022, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T20:14:38-07:00","id":1479466,"title":"","content":"Amirani Humour: Yellow Bile. (Remember, they were the precursors to the Frankensteins. This is also reflected by their Wasteland being identical to a Frankenstein's.) Their Torment comes in the form of anger at \u201cthe base nature of the world. Human depravity and injustice anger them, but so too do apathy and entropy. The world <i>should</i> be different, it <i>should</i> be better, and the Prophet knows this. Of course, it is the nature of prophecy to be ignored, and when it inevitably happens, many Amirani become bitter and resentful.<br /> <br /> Worse than being ignored, though, is when the Amirani is forced to confront his own inadequacy. Nothing infuriates him like seeing his own failures. The fire in his soul wants to move, to rise. If he is backed into a corner, and has no clear way to move forward, that fire consumes his own heart \u2014 or the people around him.<br /> <br /> When in Torment, an Amirani's body shows signs of its painful history. The head of a hanged Prophet might jerk or LOL in an unsettling way. A crucified one might manifest stigmata. A Prophet with less obvious injuries might smell strongly of brimstone, or a bystander might see a strange visions reflected in her eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> They also have the option to take a Bestowment that grants \u201cinsight into their world and the true nature of reality\u201d. It requires them to injure themselves; and for the duration of the Injury, or 24 hours, they get a bonus to all rolls that can benefit from Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T20:57:05-07:00","id":1479470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479464#post1479464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if I agree with the Torment, as I think that the Humors of Extempores rarely allow a similar Torments even when they match an established linage. I\u2019m just not seeing a overabundance of Tass as being that similar to a overabundance of Oil. The Promethean was made for a purpose, true, but I don\u2019t think Tass would reinforce what it was, just was it is currently. I don\u2019t know, that\u2019s how I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Extempore writeup's section on Torment gives examples that involve the humour existing in abundance and the humour draining away \u2014 Torment is more informed by the humour's qualities and defined by their being imbalance. Mana being a commanding/declarative/reinforcing &quot;substance&quot; that doesn't do much on its own, it seemed reasonable to link it with Purpose, particularly in relation to a Promethean made out of a spell-forged Mana-body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm\u2026There was a linage of Prophets right? What was their torment? Maybe we can use them? </div> </div> </div>The Amirani (Dark Eras Companion p98-99) were made from the bodies of people who died in agony, alchemically reinforced with metal, and they all remember their bodies catching a glimpse of a higher reality/Paradise/the Divine Fire at the moment of death. They were the yellow-bile Lineage before Frankenstein. Their Bestowment involved taking a point of aggravated damage from fire (risking Torment as normal), meditating on the visions it gives rise to, and then adding their successes on an Azoth roll to any rolls that could benefit from Willpower for 24 hours or until they heal the aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Prophets succumb to Torment when confronted with the base nature of the world. Human depravity and injustice anger them, but so too do apathy and entropy. The world <i>should</i> be different, it <i>should</i> be better, and the Prophet knows this. Of course, it is the nature of prophecy to be ignored, and when it inevitably happens, many Amirani become bitter and resentful.<br /> <br /> &quot;Worse than being ignored, though, is when the Amirani is forced to confront his own inadequacy. Nothing infuriates him like seeing his own failures. The fire in his soul wants to move, to rise. If he is backed into a corner, and has no clear way to move forward, that fire consumes his own heart \u2014 or the people around him.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certainly a direction we can go with. Hmm. Torment adding a Abyssal motif as the Promethean loses it\u2019s grip on understanding the truth is actually quite fitting. </div> </div> </div>There's a lot to work with in what overlap exists between Flux and the Abyss, to be sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Oh did your tag change? If that means you finished Hunter 1e, congratulations! Sorry if I was unobservant and that changed forever ago, or if I am seeing things. </div> </div> </div>I technically finished Hunter 1e six months ago, then had a stopover reading a couple of bluebooks and getting started at a new job. Changed the signature late last month and am currently still early in the corebook for Demon; juggling with other media means it's fallen a little by the wayside next to keeping up with ongoing feeds and clearing shorter lists, but it's been a solid reminder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T21:16:05-07:00","id":1479471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479466#post1479466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amirani Humour: Yellow Bile. (Remember, they were the precursors to the Frankensteins. This is also reflected by their Wasteland being identical to a Frankenstein's.) Their Torment comes in the form of anger at \u201cthe base nature of the world. Human depravity and injustice anger them, but so too do apathy and entropy. The world <i>should</i> be different, it <i>should</i> be better, and the Prophet knows this. Of course, it is the nature of prophecy to be ignored, and when it inevitably happens, many Amirani become bitter and resentful.<br /> <br /> Worse than being ignored, though, is when the Amirani is forced to confront his own inadequacy. Nothing infuriates him like seeing his own failures. The fire in his soul wants to move, to rise. If he is backed into a corner, and has no clear way to move forward, that fire consumes his own heart \u2014 or the people around him.<br /> <br /> When in Torment, an Amirani's body shows signs of its painful history. The head of a hanged Prophet might jerk or LOL in an unsettling way. A crucified one might manifest stigmata. A Prophet with less obvious injuries might smell strongly of brimstone, or a bystander might see a strange visions reflected in her eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> They also have the option to take a Bestowment that grants \u201cinsight into their world and the true nature of reality\u201d. It requires them to injure themselves; and for the duration of the Injury, or 24 hours, they get a bonus to all rolls that can benefit from Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! What a passage! Thank you.<br /> <br /> The Amirani Torment seems in the general area, but their relationship with Truth is consumptive, quite fitting for the Humour of Yellow Bile. Oil\u2019s poisonous nature forces confrontation with one\u2019s artificial and purposely built nature. Yellow Bile is corrosive, and it burns like fire when the world doesn\u2019t match what it should be. Tass\u2026is hidden. It pools in sacred places, and highlights the essential nature of things. In Torment, Tass flees, leaving confusion and uncertainty in its wake. Simple Truths suddenly become unclear, shrouded in mist and doubt. Every world, every symbol, becomes a riot of double meanings, if not outright deceit. One must retreat to clear ones head, but there is no clarity to be found there. Torment forces the creeping thought \u201cThe world doesn\u2019t make sense and it never did.\u201d In the darkest moments, one doubts even the veracity of the pilgrimage, wondering if it was a lie all along.<br /> <br /> I believe that works as Torment.<br /> <br /> Edit: I really need to check before I post to see if anyone else has answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-25-2022, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T21:33:51-07:00","id":1479472,"title":"","content":"You might also want to look at the Tammuz; in 2e, it was reworked to be about language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T21:52:31-07:00","id":1479473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479470#post1479470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Extempore writeup's section on Torment gives examples that involve the humour existing in abundance and the humour draining away \u2014 Torment is more informed by the humour's qualities and defined by their being imbalance. Mana being a commanding/declarative/reinforcing &quot;substance&quot; that doesn't do much on its own, it seemed reasonable to link it with Purpose, particularly in relation to a Promethean made out of a spell-forged Mana-body.</div> </div> </div> </div> Right. I think was over focusing on the practice of bloodletting as a means to drain excess humours, which was my introduction to the concept of humours. I think I\u2019ve settled on the imbalance being that the Tass drains away. That can lead a number places conceptually. I believe I\u2019m beginning see your point about Purpose, when one loses clarity, one may fall back into what one was made for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479470#post1479470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot to work with in what overlap exists between Flux and the Abyss, to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wonder if the Fire exstends into the Abyss, and if Gulmoth ever desire to be truly real\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479470#post1479470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I technically finished Hunter 1e six months ago, then had a stopover reading a couple of bluebooks and getting started at a new job. Changed the signature late last month and am currently still early in the corebook for Demon; juggling with other media means it's fallen a little by the wayside next to keeping up with ongoing feeds and clearing shorter lists, but it's been a solid reminder.</div> </div> </div> </div> Heh, sorry for the belated congratulations then. You have much more dedication than I. I meant to finish writing that tell Anathema for the Beast thread forever ago, but turns out that I\u2019m bad at juggling work life and sleep. I wish you luck on your journey though all the books.<br /> <br /> Edit: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479472#post1479472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might also want to look at the Tammuz; in 2e, it was reworked to be about language.</div> </div> </div> </div> Will do. Unfortunately, I\u2019ve in all likelihood run out of free time again. I\u2019d like to thank everyone, y\u2019all been a massive help. Hope all of you have a great day/night.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-25-2022, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T15:14:29-07:00","id":1479751,"title":"","content":"Here's my question for today.<br /> <br /> According to rules seems that any interaction with humans can be pretty dangerous to prometheans.<br /> <br /> But there's actually no way for a promethean to forge an healty relationship with the people around him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T15:31:36-07:00","id":1479753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479751#post1479751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's my question for today.<br /> <br /> According to rules seems that any interaction with humans can be pretty dangerous to prometheans.<br /> <br /> But there's actually no way for a promethean to forge an healty relationship with the people around him?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s difficult, like most things worth doing, but Promethean is a game about miracles. The True Friend merit subtracts 5 dice from any disquiet roll, and there are Transmutations to eliminate or subvert the harshness of disquiet. Sometimes someone just has enough heart to love despite the disquiet. Nothing says you can\u2019t tell your life story to the old man in the shack, and he won\u2019t sympathize. Sometimes, the world is kind. Sometimes, a flower blooms in the Wastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T17:28:30-07:00","id":1479764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479751#post1479751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's actually no way for a promethean to forge an healty relationship with the people around him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind that the Disquieted Condition doesn't progress past Stage Two without a Wasteland or an exceptional success on Disquiet rolls, any Promethean can voluntarily lower their Azoth rating with the lowered rating being the only consequence, yes, a Promethean who wishes to be around people for any length of time in an engaging fashion will eventually at least have a relatively unpleasant relationship with almost everyone who they deal with regularly.<br /> <br /> A number of Transmutations can help with this, including the Hygeius Corporeum Alembic and the Internalize Disquietism Alembic, but dice rolls are dice rolls. Unless you're extremely careful to stick to a Hovel the Wasteland will build up around you and make things worse, and being that careful is generally at odds with the experiential necessities of the Pilgrimage \u2014 you're not going to learn much about humanity if you never leave your RV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T00:20:21-07:00","id":1479795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479753#post1479753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s difficult, like most things worth doing, but Promethean is a game about miracles. The True Friend merit subtracts 5 dice from any disquiet roll, and there are Transmutations to eliminate or subvert the harshness of disquiet. Sometimes someone just has enough heart to love despite the disquiet. Nothing says you can\u2019t tell your life story to the old man in the shack, and he won\u2019t sympathize. Sometimes, the world is kind. Sometimes, a flower blooms in the Wastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember that to resolve stage 1 disquiet it s sufficient to stay away from someone for a week.<br /> I suppose you can create healty relationship with people meeting them once a week, and using phones on other days","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T00:25:10-07:00","id":1479796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479753#post1479753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The True Friend merit subtracts 5 dice from any disquiet roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can t find any rule about this.<br /> <br /> Do you mean this passage<br /> &quot;Any rolls to influence a True Friend against your character suffer a five-die penalty&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-30T08:10:14-07:00","id":1479809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479796#post1479796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can t find any rule about this.<br /> <br /> Do you mean this passage<br /> &quot;Any rolls to influence a True Friend against your character suffer a five-die penalty&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Disquiet is a supernatural effect that influences people against your character. I would very skeptical of an argument saying it didn\u2019t work. True Love empowering one to resist mind control is a common trope, this merit just facilitates that trope.<br /> <br /> Edit:Grammar","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-30-2022, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T12:50:42-07:00","id":1479971,"title":"","content":"Now an aesthetic question.<br /> <br /> I'm working on a unfleshed character born from a crash test dummy. Since dummies are usually faceless, I were wondering if the azoth illusion is so powerful to grant a functional face to a faceless promethean.<br /> <br /> And also: the unfleshed can eat food?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-02T13:17:05-07:00","id":1479972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1479971#post1479971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now an aesthetic question.<br /> <br /> I'm working on a unfleshed character born from a crash test dummy. Since dummies are usually faceless, I were wondering if the azoth illusion is so powerful to grant a functional face to a faceless promethean.<br /> <br /> And also: the unfleshed can eat food?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some extempores are made entirely of natural elements so i think that the azoth illusion are complex enough to mask these details.<br /> As for Unfleshed, nothing suggests that they doesn t share the universal digestion of other prometheans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T19:43:06-07:00","id":1488309,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, non-Osirians can Return from death once, and Osirians can do it multiple times with their special Bestowment? Do Osirians reset their lifespans every time they die and Return?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T20:43:52-07:00","id":1488312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1488309#post1488309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, non-Osirians can Return from death once, and Osirians can do it multiple times with their special Bestowment? Do Osirians reset their lifespans every time they die and Return?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct, with the caveat that Revivify gives the Osiran in question a Persistent Condition every time it's used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T03:22:20-07:00","id":1492498,"title":"","content":"Wait Osirians have absolutely no limit to the times they can resurrect? I thought it was an extra use of the generic Return, but with a Condition attached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27168-aeneas","name":"Aeneas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T04:25:49-07:00","id":1492502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeneas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1492498#post1492498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait Osirians have absolutely no limit to the times they can resurrect? I thought it was an extra use of the generic Return, but with a Condition attached.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes with a permanent change to the character each time in the form of the Persistent Condition. This is in contrast to the 1e version of the Bestowment, which allowed you to spend Azoth to resurrect other Prometheans and otherwise cost you the Bestowment to revivify yourself without resetting your Azoth to 1.<br /> <br /> Since characters can't buy more Bestowments after character creation in 2e, there wouldn't be much good in a Bestowment that you can only ever use once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T16:36:43-08:00","id":1497434,"title":"","content":"Can a Promethean be part organic, part inorganic? Specifically, if a Promethean was created using a human brain inserted into a robotic body, would it result in an Unfleshed? A Frankenstein Construct? Would it go haywire and create an Extempore? I k ow I could easily make him as a Deviant, and could even be fitting, but I kind of like the idea of a Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T16:50:55-08:00","id":1497436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1497434#post1497434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Promethean be part organic, part inorganic? Specifically, if a Promethean was created using a human brain inserted into a robotic body, would it result in an Unfleshed? A Frankenstein Construct? Would it go haywire and create an Extempore? I k ow I could easily make him as a Deviant, and could even be fitting, but I kind of like the idea of a Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd likely pin this as Unfleshed if you went Promethean, but there is a major distinction in what you're creating between a promethean or a deviant.<br /> <br /> A deviant who is a human brain integrated into a robot body is a human being who has lost their organic body and is now shoved into this foreign body, suffering from both physical and spiritual trauma and facing the threat of gradually breaking down. They are, in some meaningful sense, the same person they were when their brain was in a full human body. You could call this more like a cyborg with mostly mechanical parts.<br /> <br /> A promethean who is a human brain integrated into a robot body isn't a human being, not just in the sense that they don't have a human body but in the sense that they are not the person their brain was harvested from. That person is dead. This is a new thing brought to life by touching Divine Fire to these neural networks and robotic systems, fusing them into a living thing. It has the Azothic Memory and may have faint imprints of isolated memories or impulses left over by the brain donor, but it's not fundamentally the old person with partial amnesia, but a new creature with a few odd instincts. You could call this more like an android, but some of its parts just happen to be organic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T19:28:01-08:00","id":1497442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1497434#post1497434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Promethean be part organic, part inorganic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Three-Mile, one of the example Zeky in Night Horrors: the Tormented, has cables and tubes making up most of her throat, and tubes running out of and back into her body \u2014 most of her skin used to be an experimental hazmat suit. The rest of the section she's mentioned in likewise discusses how the Nuclear Prometheans can be biomechanical horrors \u2014 the Thin Man has a wrist-mounted cannon, and Arclight has lighting coils coming out of their body.<br /> <br /> It's a long-established thing that Prometheans can be made from corpses with nonliving materials filling in the gaps, and the Unfleshed becoming a mainstream lineage in 2e further blurs the line, albeit usually not to the degree of explicit horror as the Zeky live with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T18:07:36-08:00","id":1497591,"title":"","content":"Assuming a Centimanus has access to Vitriol and wants to restart their Pilgrimage, can they Calcify Flux Alembics? Or is that not something they can do because the Refinement of Flux has no Roles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T22:46:46-08:00","id":1497774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1497591#post1497591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a Centimanus has access to Vitriol and wants to restart their Pilgrimage, can they Calcify Flux Alembics? Or is that not something they can do because the Refinement of Flux has no Roles?</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think &quot;calcify&quot; and flux are compatable. But I could see a sort of Jovian cousin Athanor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T23:21:59-08:00","id":1497776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheStray7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1497591#post1497591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a Centimanus has access to Vitriol and wants to restart their Pilgrimage, can they Calcify Flux Alembics? Or is that not something they can do because the Refinement of Flux has no Roles?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, Centimani who'd changed their bodies with Pandoran Transmutations retained them in 1e. On the other hand, 2e models that with the Mutation Alembic's Persistent effect, which explicitly doesn't require you to retain the use of the Alembic to keep those changes.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, the entropic tilt of Flux is such that it would make sense for it to be possible for an adherent to the philosophy of the force that mutates things into uselessness to be able to permanently dedicate part of their metaphysical nature to powers built to serve that force's non-purposes. On the other hand, the easiest way to retain powers useful for Centimani is by remaining a Centimanus, particularly since instead of Role mastery Flux Alembics are gained as a function of time spend in the Refinement.<br /> <br /> I'd lean no, if only because there's no listed drawbacks of using Flux Alembics while not being a Centimanus and the one example of retaining an effect past the abandoning of the Refinement marks the permanent acquisition of entropic Transmutations as a step backwards for characters that normally have stopped tracking steps on the Pilgrimage.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T14:21:51-07:00","id":1505590,"title":"","content":"So, I finally cracked open my Prometheus book, I got, when I saw the receipt fall out, on April 20th, 2010, for $13 bucks at a local used book-store at 8:00pm (what was I doing shopping that late, besides buying beer?); it's hard for me to find a practical-use for that book besides, a fantasy RPG involving the creation of a flesh-army etc. So, could, a character with Second Sight rules create a Promethean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T19:13:54-07:00","id":1505625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1505590#post1505590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I finally cracked open my Prometheus book, I got, when I saw the receipt fall out, on April 20th, 2010, for $13 bucks at a local used book-store at 8:00pm (what was I doing shopping that late, besides buying beer?); it's hard for me to find a practical-use for that book besides, a fantasy RPG involving the creation of a flesh-army etc. So, could, a character with Second Sight rules create a Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in could a psychic or thaumaturge or cultist from that book create a Promethean? Sure. There might be some muddling given that reaching for the Divine Fire is sort of a sideways application of power from the ones more immediately available to them, but with the appropriate drive and obsession anyone can be a conduit for the Pyros to give life to one of the Created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T18:46:26-07:00","id":1506569,"title":"","content":"What does it mean when it says superficial social contact in the disquiet triggers? What does superficial social contact mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27704-money-funk","name":"Money Funk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T18:54:21-07:00","id":1506571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Money Funk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1506569#post1506569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean when it says superficial social contact in the disquiet triggers? What does superficial social contact mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think buying a bag of chips from a gas station attendant you've never met before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T20:15:24-07:00","id":1506594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Money Funk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1506569#post1506569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean when it says superficial social contact in the disquiet triggers? What does superficial social contact mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Standing in line. Sitting in front of you on the bus. Being at the same AA meeting.<br /> <br /> A scene of superficial social contact is any scene in which you're aware of the Promethean's presence and interaction below the level that would trigger Disquiet for conversing for more than a few minutes, exchanging personal information, or having rolls made for the Promethean to try to seduce/intimidate/manipulate/etc you. It's there to make Disquiet a threat even if you don't talk to anybody or do anything supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T13:24:23-07:00","id":1511265,"title":"","content":"Fun rules question I've been investigating: Can Prometheans heal naturally?<br /> <br /> Pg. 211 heavily implies that they do not with the header &quot;Mortal Healing&quot; Although the Imperatus Alembic give the persistent ability:<br /> &quot;Persistent: The Promethean has a constant flow of electricity trickling in from slight gradations of static electricity, providing a slight regenerative effect. The Created halves all healing times.&quot;<br /> In first edition it does state that Prometheans heal like mortals.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T14:04:28-07:00","id":1511278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1511265#post1511265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun rules question I've been investigating: Can Prometheans heal naturally?<br /> <br /> Pg. 211 heavily implies that they do not with the header &quot;Mortal Healing&quot; Although the Imperatus Alembic give the persistent ability:<br /> &quot;Persistent: The Promethean has a constant flow of electricity trickling in from slight gradations of static electricity, providing a slight regenerative effect. The Created halves all healing times.&quot;<br /> In first edition it does state that Prometheans heal like mortals.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They can. I made the error when I put up my combat thread and had it pointed out to me that they can-I'll get you a page citation when I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T20:54:28-07:00","id":1511326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1511278#post1511278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can. I made the error when I put up my combat thread and had it pointed out to me that they can-I'll get you a page citation when I can.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501082-let-s-talk-about-combat-in-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1501092#post1501092\">This'un here</a>, now that I'm not on mobile.<br /> <br /> (We apparently saw this question at the same time, because I saw your reply while I was searching for the thread to get the post.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T03:22:32-07:00","id":1522785,"title":"","content":"Ok, teo not entirely related questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> Can human alchemists use flux?<br /> <br /> And can a Promethean who has become human then become an Alchemist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T03:54:43-07:00","id":1522786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1522785#post1522785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, teo not entirely related questions:<br /> <br /> <br /> Can human alchemists use flux?<br /> <br /> And can a Promethean who has become human then become an Alchemist?</div> </div> </div> </div>In night horror the tormented an Alchemist uses Lordship, so i would say yes<br /> <br /> Alchemy can be learned by normal humans, and a Promethean becomes a normal human after the New dawn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T05:42:29-07:00","id":1522788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1522786#post1522786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In night horror the tormented an Alchemist uses Lordship, so i would say yes<br /> <br /> Alchemy can be learned by normal humans, and a Promethean becomes a normal human after the New dawn</div> </div> </div> </div>Would a former Promethean have an advantage learning alchemy (if they remembered their past) or disadvantaged (not being able to manipulate Pyros the way they used to with their body)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T06:59:33-07:00","id":1522792,"title":"","content":"A former Promethean would be disadvantaged compared to a Promethean because they can't manipulate Pyros the way they used to. They don't get an advantage, because Prometheans don't learn alchemy; they <i>are </i>alchemy. Its used is so introduce to them that they don't really know how they do what they do \u2014 which makes it difficult for them to teach anyone else, including their future (human) selves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T09:07:09-07:00","id":1522796,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that the most alchemist-adjacent Refinement's associated Condition for its unique Transmutations makes them functionally an alchemist for the purposes of Pyros expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T01:45:43-07:00","id":1522817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1522792#post1522792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A former Promethean would be disadvantaged compared to a Promethean because they can't manipulate Pyros the way they used to. They don't get an advantage, because Prometheans don't learn alchemy; they <i>are </i>alchemy. Its used is so introduce to them that they don't really know how they do what they do \u2014 which makes it difficult for them to teach anyone else, including their future (human) selves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes,but advantages compared to a human who doesn't know alchemy is possible.<br /> <br /> They may even have seen human alchemists in their past life as a Promethean.<br /> <br /> But maybe disadvantaged because they have seen what happens to human alchemists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth pointing out that the most alchemist-adjacent Refinement's associated Condition for its unique Transmutations makes them functionally an alchemist for the purposes of Pyros expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure i understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T03:17:28-07:00","id":1522818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1522817#post1522817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes,but advantages compared to a human who doesn't know alchemy is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone is an alchemist, they know that alchemy is possible. Also, many ex-Prometheans don't remember their former existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-20-2023, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T05:21:41-07:00","id":1522822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1522817#post1522817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure i understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Flawed Vessel Condition one can get from Alchemicus Transmutations messes with a Promethean's ability to retain and spend Pyros, so a Promethean who spent time in the Refinement of Mercury could easily have experience dealing with some of the operative limits of a mortal alchemist prior to the New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T18:17:23-08:00","id":1527402,"title":"","content":"Has a vampire, in game, ever drank from a Promie and got disquiet? If so, how'd they deal with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T07:09:01-08:00","id":1527423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1527402#post1527402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has a vampire, in game, ever drank from a Promie and got disquiet? If so, how'd they deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Player guide for the Contagion suggest inflicting a lethal damage for every two point of vitae ingested if i remember it correctly, but i can totally see a feeding scene as a trigger for a disquiet roll.<br /> i think that the disquiet filled vampire would simply avoid such &quot;spicy&quot; meal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T13:36:22-07:00","id":1534369,"title":"","content":"What is the dice pool for Biting Aura? The description sais none, but still lists roll results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-17T18:13:29-07:00","id":1534380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1534369#post1534369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the dice pool for Biting Aura? The description sais none, but still lists roll results.</div> </div> </div> </div>My copy says Presence + Azoth. You may need to update your copy to the one that has &quot;(Final Download)&quot; in the filename by <a href=\"https://preview.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/189395/Promethean-the-Created-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">redownloading it from DTRPG</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-27T18:15:43-07:00","id":1537806,"title":"","content":"If a second pabdoran in a pack becomes a sublimati is the Centimati or Sublimati who leads the pack most likely to accept them as a more valued subordinate or expell them???<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My guess is a rank 4 or 5 Sublimati is probaly not going to see them as a threat onee of llower rank its a biit more iffy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T04:01:05-07:00","id":1544786,"title":"","content":"Player guide to the Contagion suggest that a Major splat could gain a minor splat if it is from &quot;another book&quot; (for example a Non Vampire could became a ghoul).<br /> <br /> On Promethean core book one of the suggested condition to master the Scientist role is to replicate human alchemy<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> Do you think that a Promethean could buy dots of Magnitude and became an Alchemist?<br /> What are alternatives ways to do it? (I could think of merits like<br /> Blood Chymistry, could it work?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T20:33:48-08:00","id":1545430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1544786#post1544786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player guide to the Contagion suggest that a Major splat could gain a minor splat if it is from &quot;another book&quot; (for example a Non Vampire could became a ghoul).<br /> <br /> On Promethean core book one of the suggested condition to master the Scientist role is to replicate human alchemy<br /> <br /> So...<br /> <br /> Do you think that a Promethean could buy dots of Magnitude and became an Alchemist?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because Magnitude exists for the twofold purposes of allowing Pyros alchemists to use Transmutations and serving as a downgrade when Alchemicus Transmutations apply the Flawed Vessel Condition.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are alternatives ways to do it? (I could think of merits like Blood Chymistry, could it work?) </div> </div> </div>As described in the writeup for Magnitude, the mechanics of alchemy are accomplished using Attributes and Skills. &quot;Alchemy&quot; is an example Occult Specialty.<br /> <br /> The sample Scientist milestone is not mechanically defined for obvious reasons, but &quot;perform a series of extended actions centered on the Science and/or Occult Skills to replicate a feat of alchemy like creating a homunculus, changin one precious metal into another, or other alchemical effects Prometheans would more conventionally accomplish using Transmutations&quot; is the gist of what it's getting at \u2014 it's the Refinement of Quicksilver's most ready justification for doing stuff that looks like Mad Science even though its signature Transmutation can accomplish similar effects with a touch and no special equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T12:23:35-07:00","id":1554165,"title":"","content":"&quot;That, &quot;Thing&quot;, in the castle&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, sometime in the 18th-century, a vampire-prince complained about a promie actually ruling a mortal-city. Now, is that even possible? With disquiet? Can a promie actually act in a political-office of a human-city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-05T13:07:50-07:00","id":1554170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554165#post1554165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;That, &quot;Thing&quot;, in the castle&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, sometime in the 18th-century, a vampire-prince complained about a promie actually ruling a mortal-city. Now, is that even possible? With disquiet? Can a promie actually act in a political-office of a human-city?</div> </div> </div> </div>The bigger issue in the modern urban era is that Prometheans have no legal identity upon which to base a political career. Careful use of Disquietism, maintaining a Hovel, keeping the Fire Dampened, and conducting business indirectly can theoretically allow one of the Created to run a community for a good while if they can get past that hurdle (such as through the Assimilation and Doppelganger Deception Alembics) or are operating in a time and place where documented identification is less of a concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T18:54:35-07:00","id":1554248,"title":"","content":"I'm not thinking modern, but, Age of Enlightenment: 1700s. Just a thought of another supernatural running a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T19:35:44-07:00","id":1554252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554248#post1554248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not thinking modern, but, Age of Enlightenment: 1700s. Just a thought of another supernatural running a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logistics of running a city, coupled with the general rarity of supernaturals overall and Prometheans in particular, means that part is comparatively straightforward, provided you can build up a functional support system, make inroads with the locals, and/or falsify the background necessary to keep people from asking too many questions.<br /> <br /> Open rule without carefully controlling visitors and appearances will be trickier, and Torment is in some ways the bigger issue than Disquiet (methods of resolving Torment are thin on the ground, it's harder to resist in a Wasteland, and one of the means of clearing the Condition is forming a Wasteland, which also makes Disquiet a bigger threat over time).<br /> <br /> Some of this is also down to running a city being hard; the types of supernatural creature most associated with it have cults dedicated to them or lean heavily into Social Merits and Merits that give them free Social Merits as part of their connections with other monsters, and Prometheans are neither of those things, but the tools exist for one of the Created to at least make a good showing of it for long enough that an inopportune qashmal, Pandoran, Firestorm, or other wrinkle can make a grander than usual catastrophe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-09T03:22:42-07:00","id":1554255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554165#post1554165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;That, &quot;Thing&quot;, in the castle&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, sometime in the 18th-century, a vampire-prince complained about a promie actually ruling a mortal-city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that quote from? Some context might help answer your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T06:38:51-07:00","id":1554660,"title":"","content":"Daily silly question: Even the &quot;True Friend&quot; is affected by disquietism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T07:39:17-07:00","id":1554661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554660#post1554660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daily silly question: Even the &quot;True Friend&quot; is affected by disquietism?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not immune to Disquiet, though the nature of how the Disquieted Condition works means the player of the character who has the True Friend is by definition making any decisions about what Disquiet causes them to do, and a case can be made for the -5 penalty to rolls to influence them against the Promethean applying to rolls to worsen Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T08:57:30-07:00","id":1554664,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> If everything goes well, I will be in a Promethean chronicle really soon, and I'm a bit worried about the Disquiet and it's effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T10:28:32-07:00","id":1554665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554664#post1554664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> If everything goes well, I will be in a Promethean chronicle really soon, and I'm a bit worried about the Disquiet and it's effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my experience if at least 2 different promethean are in a throng and moderately careful (like using Disquietism Transmutation), the Disquiet problem will start to kick in from Azoth 4-5, not before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T12:16:21-07:00","id":1554667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554665#post1554665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my experience if at least 2 different promethean are in a throng and moderately careful (like using Disquietism Transmutation), the Disquiet problem will start to kick in from Azoth 4-5, not before</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth remembering that 2e both allows you to lower your effective Azoth (whether by Dampening the Fire or using a Hovel) and only allows Disquiet to reach contagious levels in a Wasteland or with exceptional success on a roll of just Azoth modified by your throngmates' Lineages and contested by Resolve + Composure; unless you're specifically working on something that requires higher levels of Azoth or a lot of Pyros, you can putter along in power-saving mode and minimize repeated contact with the same people, particularly given that all the effects of Disquieted beyond the Social penalties and increased Doors are triggered by the Promethean player's decision at a rate of no more than once per session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T18:26:34-07:00","id":1554675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554660#post1554660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daily silly question: Even the &quot;True Friend&quot; is affected by disquietism?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also relevant to ponder that the effect of <i>Disquiet</i> in the fiction isn't necessarily open hostility or enmity.<br /> <br /> The person affected becomes irritable and <i>prone</i> to blame the Promethean on things, but that's just a surface level (even if quite intense) emotional response. They're still in control of their minds and are free to decide on how to act upon it. Up to and including being aware of the problem and able to look for ways to mitigate it, if they know what's going on.<br /> <br /> A <b>True Friend</b> is likely to stay at your side just as much as without <i>Disquiet</i>, unless the player deliberately chooses otherwise, no need for adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T03:59:47-07:00","id":1554764,"title":"","content":"I may be prone to play a unfleshed. One of those humanoid robots like Tesla's ones.<br /> <br /> Now the matter is: how far the Azoth disfigurement can go? My character can eat without an actual mouth? And if his real hands have no fingers, the Azoth-made fingers will feel real and functional?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T09:31:55-07:00","id":1554776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554764#post1554764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the matter is: how far the Azoth disfigurement can go? My character can eat without an actual mouth? And if his real hands have no fingers, the Azoth-made fingers will feel real and functional?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character's disfigurements are their real body as a Promethean. The thing that makes people treat them as human is an aura of normalcy that flickers when they spend Pyros. If you don't have a mouth, you can't put food in it nor swallow it for sustenance, and if your hands don't have fingers you aren't going to be dextrous enough to manipulate things like someone with fingers could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T09:50:41-07:00","id":1554777,"title":"","content":"So if my character is an unfleshed robot he cannot eat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T16:37:35-07:00","id":1554801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554777#post1554777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if my character is an unfleshed robot he cannot eat?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make your character without some means of putting food in them they cannot eat. Most Unfleshed have mouths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T19:53:21-07:00","id":1554810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554777#post1554777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if my character is an unfleshed robot he cannot eat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character has a functional mouth, period, even if it is literally a tear in the metal.<br /> <br /> Unfleshed still have human-enough bodies, this much is a requirement (as far as requirements go for Prometheans). You have normal human needs and the physical means to act on them.<br /> <br /> The secret to understand a Promethean is to know that you're not simply animated material, you're a human being, even if an artificial one. You're not human-like, you're not human-looking, you're not disguised as human, you're human <i>sans</i> soul. You're the result of an Alchemical transmutation into a human body.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Divine Fire being what it is, exceptions exist for everything. But then exceptions must be treated as such, they require special considerations and rules. Even then, any aspect of your true body is real and you have to deal with it, people just won't perceive it as inhuman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T10:23:03-07:00","id":1554854,"title":"","content":"Even unfleshed have human needs? This kills my character concept a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 10-30-2025, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T11:51:46-07:00","id":1554858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554854#post1554854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even unfleshed have human needs? This kills my character concept a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ways in which Prometheans consistently differ from humans (unless your game includes specific exceptions) are described in the section on Superlative Endurance on pages 169-170 of the 2e corebook. Anything else is a Merit, Bestowment, or other mechanically or narratively added wrinkle. The Fire needs fuel and the Created are pursuing humanity at a deeper level than superficial shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-30T12:36:20-07:00","id":1554865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554854#post1554854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even unfleshed have human needs? This kills my character concept a little.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> pointed the page, but in short, yes.<br /> <br /> Long explanation, all Prometheans are made of non-living components, were it just about animation they wouldn't have human needs, either.<br /> <br /> The game is about Alchemy as a process of transformation from one thing into another, and the Prometheans themselves transformed from non-living matter (organic or not) into new living beings. They're <b>all</b> alive in every sense of the word. The Pilgrimage is the remaining process, which is the transformation of Azoth into a true soul.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Barring some trait that specifically says otherwise, your body is human even though it shouldn't be, and it has a mostly human biology. There's some nuance, but that's the gist of it no matter the character. You eat, drink, breath, piss, sweat, everything.<br /> <br /> You may talk to your ST, though, for any exception you want to be, there are plenty of them. As an example, you may make an Extempore that isn't becoming human, but something else, and have the lack of human needs as a unique Bestowment, but then you have to negotiate it with your ST.<br /> <br /> Promethean is open-ended in this regard. The Azoth has some regularities, but ultimately it is unpredictability incarnate. You just have to understand what are the core assumptions before you make a character that breaks them. You could even in theory argue a character that's mechanically some other splat and yet is in reality an Extempore, it would just require some adaptations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T03:15:15-07:00","id":1554891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554854#post1554854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even unfleshed have human needs? This kills my character concept a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the other have said, BUT see the Persistent effect of the Motus transmutation coupled with the sleepless merit.<br /> Also consider that by standard rules all prometheans... don t need a toilet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T09:13:19-07:00","id":1554892,"title":"","content":"Thank you to everyone, now I think I can refine better the backstory of my character, lastly: even a demiurge can feel the disquiet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T09:25:36-07:00","id":1554893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1222410-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-prometheans-edition?p=1554892#post1554892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lastly: even a demiurge can feel the disquiet?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Postpartum,&quot; a section on the second page of Chapter Two, describes how Disquiet may begin in a Promethean's demiurge, and Victor Frankenstein's reaction to his creation is one of the classic examples of that Lineage's Disquiet. Disquiet affects every human the Promethean interacts with in the absence of a specific quality that prevents it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-31T16:21:58-07:00","id":1554901,"title":"","content":"Only keep in mind that not all <i>Demiurges</i> are necessarily human. So it isn't impossible for a given <i>Demiurge</i> to be something immune to <i>Disquite</i>.<br /> <br /> Barring that, though, they're affected as normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}